  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This project was created for No Translation Required: Artists Books in Germany and Georgia a class in conjunction with Savannah College of Art &amp; Design and the Hochschule für bildende Künste Braunschweig. Over the course of three weeks ten American SCAD Students spent time viewing Germany's premier artists books with several students from the HBK. Several /// cultures were noticed and discussed during this experience, ranging form design methodology, personal style and simple lifestyle choices. Slowly but shurely the students began to /// language barriers. While there may be serveral [sic] different view points it became very apparent that we all share the same human condition. We can all understand and process simple /// recognize a borad [sic] spectrum of human emotion. Receiving a smile from a stranger on the street, expressions of stress, anger, hapiness [sic] and love all look the same in America or Germany." -- Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
